 "description": "Arctic sea ice, one day per frame, from 16 Apr 2021 to 15 Apr 2023: two full years of melt and freeze-up seen from above the North Pole (JAXA AMSR2, 15 % concentration). The flute is the sea-ice extent measured from the movie: more ice plays higher. It falls through each summer to a low in September and climbs back each winter, twice. A bowed-glass pad an octave and more below plays the 1981-2010 median extent for the same day, so the gap between them is the ice that is missing. Ocean and wind grow as water opens. The audio runs 1.5 times slower than the movie.",
